---
import Layout from '@/layouts/LoginLayout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Changelog | Almstins"
  description="What's new, what changed, and why — updates from the Almstins team."
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="page">

    <header class="page-header">
      <a href="/login" class="back-link">← Back to Almstins</a>
    </header>

    <main class="content">
      <h1 class="page-title">Changelog</h1>
      <p class="page-sub">What's new, what changed, and why.</p>

      <div class="entries">

        <article class="entry">
          <time class="entry-date">May 21, 2026</time>
          <div class="entry-body">
            <p>Each tin on the vault dashboard now has a small corner flag that tells you what you're looking at at a glance. Wallet tins get a chain-colored triangle — gold for Bitcoin, silver for Ethereum, violet for Solana, and so on — with a chain-link icon. Exchange tins (Coinbase, Kraken, Gemini, etc.) get a muted fold with a bank icon instead. The colors match each chain's established identity, so once you learn them you don't have to read the label.</p>
            <p>The "What's new" link on the home page has moved to the right side of the screen, below the portfolio preview, where it has room to breathe.</p>
            <p>The wallet checker is now available in Spanish at <a href="/wallet-checker/es">/wallet-checker/es</a> — fully translated including all threat explanations, modals, verdict labels, FAQ, and safety tips. Crypto terms like wallet, token, phishing, and honeypot are kept in English, which is how the Spanish-speaking crypto community actually uses them.</p>
            <p>Language toggles (🇪🇸 En Español / 🇺🇸 In English) now appear on all four pages: the main landing page, the Spanish landing page, the English wallet checker, and the Spanish wallet checker. One tap to switch languages from anywhere.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="entry">
          <time class="entry-date">May 16, 2026</time>
          <div class="entry-body">
            <p>Yesterday I had a chance to watch a friend use my demo for the first time. He was on his computer, while I looked over his shoulder. Seeing it through fresh eyes was clarifying.</p>
            <p>So this morning I went to work. Instead of walking you, my visitors, through a how-to, I stripped it back. The goal is simple: I want to show you what's waiting when you sign up.</p>
            <p>I seeded the demo with realistic numbers across exchanges and wallets, labeled the key sections so nothing feels mysterious, and refreshed the front page. The wallet lookup is still there — paste any address and see what's inside, no account needed — but I moved it out of the spotlight. The more important thing is that you can see the value before logging in and watching your own numbers fill the tins.</p>
            <p>More updates coming as the project grows. I would welcome any feedback through the portal on the login page, or email me directly at <a href="mailto:hello@almstins.com">hello@almstins.com</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </main>

  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2rem) 6rem;
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .back-link {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: rgba(165,180,252,0.7);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .back-link:hover { color: #a5b4fc; }

  .page-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #f5f8ff;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .page-sub {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: rgba(245,248,255,0.45);
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .entries {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .entry {
    border-left: 2px solid rgba(45,212,168,0.35);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .entry-date {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: rgba(45,212,168,0.8);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .entry-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }
  .entry-body p {
    font-size: 0.975rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgba(245,248,255,0.8);
  }
  .entry-body a {
    color: rgba(45,212,168,0.9);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .entry-body a:hover { color: rgb(45,212,168); }
</style>
